  "learn": {
    "title": "Climate Display",
    "body": "Connect BME280 VIN to 3V3, GND to GND, SDA to A4 and SCL to A5. Connect LCD VCC to 5V, GND to GND, SDA to A4 and SCL to A5. The bus is shared, but addresses differ: BME280 0x76 and LCD 0x27. This teaching model abstracts I²C pull-up voltages; verify pull-ups and level compatibility on physical modules.\n\nInitialize Adafruit_BME280 and LiquidCrystal_I2C(0x27, 16, 2). Every 250 ms, read temperature and humidity, clear the old text and show T=24.5 C on row 0 and H=55.0 % on row 1 using one decimal place. Also print the two readings to Serial.\n\nRun at the default 24.5°C / 55% first, then use the BME280 inspector to set 31°C / 70%. Both LCD rows must change to T=31.0 C and H=70.0 %. A display containing fixed strings cannot follow the sensor.",
    "links": []
